```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Tool-calling LLM agents with fast, cancellable tools where tool latency ≤ arg-decode time (r ≤ 1) and leading-arg prediction correctness ≥0.6-0.8; e.g., local function calls, cached DB lookups, or idempotent low-latency APIs. Not the high-latency tool regime (r ≥ 2) emphasized in the claim.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only for the claimed high-tool-latency regime; modest conditional win (10-25% step speedup at r=0.5) only in the low-latency regime where "the absolute time saved is small" (packet). L0 is an analytic latency model with swept parameters (252 configs, MC-validated), no GPU, no real agent traces, and no measured speculation-correctness p_correct. The win region (r < 1) has "the *least* tool latency to overlap" (packet).
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Need p_correct ≥0.92-0.97 for r ≥ 2 to break even (packet: "At r=8 you need >0.92 correctness just to break even"); Most production tools are side-effecting/non-cancellable, incurring w=1 (full wasted work) or w>1 rollback cost; Structural saturation: upside S = min((1-lead)·t_args, t_tool) caps while penalty P = w·t_tool grows linearly with tool latency, driving p* → 1; Higher lead fraction (more decoded before firing) raises p* because it shrinks overlappable decode (packet); No real-trace measurement of p_correct on agent workloads — "THE unknown that decides everything" (packet); Commit/validation overhead c_commit unmeasured in production; Prior-art sweep not performed — speculative execution under misprediction penalty is classic CS pattern (branch prediction, speculative I/O, LLM speculative decoding)]
RATIONALE: Packet EXP-0004 shows break-even p* = 0.76-0.97 for r ≥ 2 (the "headline regime in the claim") and states "The honest-negative branch in pre-registration fires: wasted-work dominates in the interesting regime" (packet). For r ≥ 2, "need p* ≈ 0.76–0.97. At r=8 you need >0.92 correctness just to break even, and full wins (>10%) need p≈0.99" (packet). The only robust win is at r ≲ 1 where "tool latency is comparable to or smaller than the remaining arg-decode — but that is the regime with the least latency to overlap, so the absolute benefit is modest" (packet). L0 evidence is model-only: "no GPU/network" and "The deciding unknown is REAL p_correct on agent traces" (packet). Without measured p_correct from real agent traces, operational significance remains unproven for production deployment.
```
